  "id": "pr-280",
  "instruction": "The CLI must support a `--scalar` option for glom transformations run against JSON, YAML, TOML, or Python target data supplied through command-line arguments, files, or standard input. With this option, a scalar result—such as a string, number, boolean, or null—is emitted as plain scalar text: string values must not include JSON quotes, and the output must not contain surrounding whitespace or an automatically added trailing newline. When the result is a collection, including an object or array, `--scalar` must fall back to the existing normal JSON output rather than flattening the collection. Without `--scalar`, existing JSON output behavior must remain unchanged, and existing input, spec, format, and error handling must continue to work.",
